prompts.prompt_text:
Summarize the following article into 3 punchy sentences for Twitter/X. Use active voice, include the key insight, and end with a hook. Max 280 characters total.

Article:
{{article_text}}

Write an SEO meta description for the following article. Rules: exactly 140-160 characters, include the primary keyword naturally, make it compelling with a clear benefit, no clickbait. Output ONLY the description, nothing else.

Article title: {{title}}
Article summary: {{summary}}
Primary keyword: {{keyword}}

I got this error:

```
{{error_message}}
```

Context: {{what_i_was_doing}}
Language: {{language}}
Framework: {{framework}}

Explain:
1. What this error means in plain English
2. The most likely cause
3. Step-by-step fix
4. How to prevent it in the future

Write a regex pattern that matches: {{description}}

Examples that SHOULD match:
{{match_examples}}

Examples that should NOT match:
{{no_match_examples}}

Provide:
1. The regex pattern
2. A line-by-line explanation of each part
3. Test it against all examples above
4. Note any edge cases or limitations

Write a professional email for this situation:

Situation: {{situation}}
Recipient: {{recipient}}
Tone: {{tone}} (formal/friendly/direct)
Key message: {{main_point}}
Desired action: {{what_you_want}}

Keep it under 150 words. Subject line included. No filler phrases like 'I hope this email finds you well'.

Write a product description for:

Product: {{product_name}}
Key features: {{features}}
Target audience: {{audience}}
Price point: {{price}}

Structure:
1. Headline (benefit-driven, under 10 words)
2. Opening hook (address the pain point)
3. 3-5 key benefits (not features)
4. Social proof suggestion
5. Call to action

Tone: {{tone}}. Max 200 words.
